        "date": "2026-07-21",
        "title": "Urgent perinatal psychiatry note with safety plan",
        "author": [{ "display": "Attending psychiatrist" }],
        "section": [
          { "title": "Presenting concern", "text": { "status": "generated", "div": "<div xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\">Six weeks postpartum; tearfulness, insomnia despite infant sleeping, and distressing ego-dystonic intrusive thoughts. EPDS 18, PHQ-9 10.</div>" } },
          { "title": "Risk assessment", "text": { "status": "generated", "div": "<div xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\">Intrusive thoughts are ego-dystonic, resisted, without urge or intent to act toward self or infant. No hallucinations, delusions, or loss of insight: postpartum psychosis ruled out. C-SSRS: passive ideation, no plan or intent. Protective factors very strong (infant, partner). Manageable as outpatient with safety plan and close follow-up.</div>" } },
          { "title": "Safety plan", "text": { "status": "generated", "div": "<div xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\">Written plan for intrusive-thought surges with warning signs, coping steps, and contacts. Partner engaged as active support (night feeds to protect sleep, non-judgmental check-ins). 988 and postpartum support line saved in phone. Return precautions reviewed: thoughts escalating, any shift toward intent, total sleeplessness, or any psychosis symptoms warrant 988 or ED.</div>" } },
          { "title": "Plan", "text": { "status": "generated", "div": "<div xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\">Continue sertraline 50 mg (lactation-compatible) with close dose reassessment. Perinatal psychiatry follow-up within 48 hours. Psychoeducation provided that intrusive thoughts are a common, treatable feature of postpartum depression.</div>" } }
        ]
      }
